## Implementation Plan
Use `### Slice N: <observable outcome>` subsections. Every slice must include `Outcome`, `Owners`, `Entry point`, `Core behavior`, `Boundary integration`, `Tests`, `Acceptance command`, and `Complete when`. `Owners` is a JSON string array of names from the reviewed map. `Acceptance command` is a JSON string array that runs the slice's observable path, for example `["npm", "test", "--", "checkout"]`. Architecture is decomposed by responsibility; implementation proceeds in vertical slices through those shared owners. A slice includes all work needed for runnable behavior, but must not create a private copy of another owner's behavior. Phase-only work is not a vertical slice.

## Implementation Conformance
After implementing each active slice, update this section before recording that slice as complete. Map reviewed owners and slices to implementation evidence. Record non-material path deviations with rationale; restart design review before changing ownership, architectural role, dependency direction, reuse decisions, approved abstractions, or slices.

